<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia mulls int'l bond to cover budget deficit.</title>
<headline>Slovakia mulls int'l bond to cover budget deficit.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak Finance Ministry on Friday said it was considering issuing an unspecified tranche of international bonds later this year to help cover its 1997 planned budget deficit.</p>
<p>&quot;We have this opportunity (to issue an international bond), and we are thinking about it,&quot; Marian Horvath, head of the ministry's State Assets and Liabilities Department, told Reuters.</p>
</text>
